        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What were you called to on {DATE}?", "\"A house fire in the early morning. Crews were already on scene when I arrived, and a firefighter had been burned on the hand and neck.\""), .direct("What did you determine about the cause?", "\"I found gasoline at the back door. The burn pattern started there and moved inward, which tells me an accelerant was poured and lit.\""), .direct("Who had lived at the house?", "\"{D} had been evicted two days earlier. The eviction order was served and {D.he} was told to be out by that date.\""), .direct("What did the neighbor's camera show?", "\"A figure at the back door at 2:30 a.m., about fifteen minutes before the fire started. The figure's face is not visible.\""), .direct("What did you learn about gasoline purchases?", "\"A station camera shows {DL} buying gasoline at 12:30 a.m. that night. A gas can in {DL}'s truck had soot on it.\""), .direct("How was the firefighter hurt?", "\"At about 3:10 a.m. a flashover caught the firefighter on the hand and neck. The injuries were painful burns that needed treatment.\""), .cross("Isn't it true you can't identify the figure on the neighbor's camera?", "\"Correct. The image is dark, and the figure is partly turned away. I can't say it's {DL}.\""), .cross("Did you find {D} at the scene?", "\"No. {DL} was not there. {DL} was located later and said {D.he} was staying with a friend.\""), .cross("Is soot on a gas can unusual?", "\"Not very. A can kept near a fire or a grill could pick up soot, and I can't say when it got there.\""), .cross("Did you check the defendant's phone location?", "\"The router log of the friend's Wi-Fi showed {DL}'s phone connected until about 3 a.m. I can't tell you whether the phone stayed with {DL}.\""), .cross("Was gasoline in the defendant's truck tank or a can?", "\"A can. {D.He} said {D.he} bought gas for the truck and carried a can for it, and I can't prove otherwise.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's friend",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"{D} is a good friend. I let {DF} stay on my couch after the eviction, because {D.he} had nowhere else to go.\""), .direct("What did you see the night of the fire?", "\"{D.He} arrived after midnight with a bag of food and a can in the truck. We played games and watched TV into the night.\""), .direct("Where was the defendant's phone?", "\"On my Wi-Fi. I have a router that logs connected devices, and it shows {D.his} phone on my network until about 3 a.m.\""), .direct("Did the defendant leave your apartment?", "\"Not that I saw. I went to bed around 2 and {D.he} was still on the couch with the TV on.\""), .direct("How was the defendant acting?", "\"Tired and frustrated about the eviction, but not angry at anyone in particular. {D.He} talked about finding a new place.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say about the house?", "\"That {D.he} was sorry to lose it, but it was out of {D.his} hands. {D.He} didn't mention anything about revenge.\""), .cross("You went to bed around 2, correct?", "\"Yes. After that I was asleep, and I can't say what {D.he} did for the next hour.\""), .cross("A router log shows a phone, not a person, doesn't it?", "\"That's true. It shows the phone connected. I can't say who was holding it.\""), .cross("Did you hear the truck start up that night?", "\"No. I sleep in a back room with a fan, and I wouldn't have heard it.\""), .cross("You didn't see {D} buy gasoline?", "\"No. {D.He} mentioned filling the truck when {D.he} came in, but I never saw a can.\""), .cross("You and the defendant are close friends, aren't you?", "\"Yes. I care about {D.him}, and I'm telling you only what I know.\"")],
