        openings: ("{D} was evicted from a house, and two days later at 2:45 a.m. gasoline was poured at its back door and lit. A figure appears at that door at 2:30, a gas can with soot was found in {D}'s truck, and a firefighter was burned on the hand and neck.", "{D} was sleeping on a friend's couch, with a phone on that friend's Wi-Fi until 3 a.m., and the camera shows no face. The defense says anger over an eviction and a can in a truck are not proof of who lit that fire."),
